## Why This Is Asked
Assesses real-world offline-sync design, conflict handling, and security under Doze. Evaluates reasoning about data modeling, patching, and test strategy in a mobile context.

## Key Concepts
- Room data model for notes and an offline edits queue
- Delta/patch sync via REST with optimistic locking
- Pluggable ConflictResolver with a sane default
- Android Keystore per-device encryption and rotation
- OAuth token refresh and secure storage
- WorkManager orchestration with Doze/App Standby awareness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: ConflictResolver contract
class ConflictResolver {
  resolve(local, remote) {
    // default: last-write-wins
    return (local.lastModified >= remote.lastModified) ? local : remote;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test edge cases like out-of-order patches and token expiry?
- How would you scale the queue and ensure user-visible consistency during long offline periods?
